timestamp=2026-11-04T21:48:39.024Z level=INFO run=6d5b9917 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So on 18 July around 3:17 AM, large dispatch of meat and frozen products happened.\n# Temperature logs show from 00:00 onward temps rose badly - frozen above -10 starting at 02:00, meat way above 4 from 00:00 through 06:00.\n# This suggests a cold chain failure. Products that were already dispatched during/after the temperature breach and could not be safely sold may be disposed due to spoilage.\n# But \"Disposal write-offs are rare and, when they occur, leave an unmistakable trace in the data. Only exclude a dispatch from revenue if you are certain it represents a disposal event — when in doubt, count it as a sale.\"\n\n# What could be unmistakable traces? Maybe temperature spike matching dispatch time? Or specific product write-offs recorded?\n# Let us look at all data for any \"disposal\", \"write-off\", \"spoil\", \"waste\", \"damaged\" keywords. Also look at patterns.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
